Enhancement: Add options to configure SSH keepalive for SFTP backend

SFTP connections could be interrupted when no data was sent for a long time,
for example while restic processes large amounts of unchanged data. The new
`sftp.server-alive-interval` and `sftp.server-alive-count-max` options set the
corresponding `ServerAliveInterval` and `ServerAliveCountMax` SSH options to
keep the connection alive. If unset, the values from the SSH configuration
are used.

